## Message-Command to Project-Rule-Parameter Mapping

| Message-Command | Project-Rule-Parameter | Purpose |
|-----------------|------------------------|---------|
| `verify-official-documentation` | @workflows/documentation-workflow/documentation-verification.mdc | Verify documentation against implementation |
| `create-official-documentation` | @workflows/documentation-workflow/documentation-creation.mdc | Create new documentation following standards |
| `update-documentation-format` | @workflows/documentation-workflow/format-standardization.mdc | Update format to match documentation standards |
| `documentation-status` | @workflows/documentation-workflow/documentation-status.mdc | Report on documentation coverage and accuracy |
| `create-template` | @workflows/documentation-workflow/template-creation.mdc | Create documentation templates by type |

## Usage Examples

### Documentation Verification Workflow

```
verify-official-documentation: official-documentation/front-end/wallet-integration.md @workflows/documentation-workflow/documentation-verification.mdc
```

This message-command verifies the wallet integration documentation against implementation using the guidance in documentation-verification.mdc.

### Documentation Creation Workflow

```
create-official-documentation: official-documentation/back-end/transaction-api.md @workflows/documentation-workflow/documentation-creation.mdc
```

This message-command provides guidance for creating new transaction API documentation using the patterns in documentation-creation.mdc.

### Format Standardization Workflow

```
update-documentation-format: official-documentation/blockchain/wallet.md @workflows/documentation-workflow/format-standardization.mdc
```

This message-command updates the wallet documentation format using the guidance in format-standardization.mdc.

## Combined Tools and Project-Rule-Parameters

Certain complex workflows benefit from combining tools from different sources:

### Documentation with Markdown Tools

```
create-official-documentation: official-documentation/architecture/system-overview.md @workflows/documentation-workflow/documentation-creation.mdc @parameters/tool/markdown-patterns.mdc
```

This combines documentation creation patterns with markdown-specific patterns.

### Documentation with Code Examples

```
create-official-documentation: official-documentation/front-end/api-client.md @workflows/documentation-workflow/documentation-creation.mdc @parameters/tool/code-example-patterns.mdc
```

This combines documentation creation patterns with code example formatting techniques.

## File Structure Requirements

All 1000xbrain files referenced as project-rule-parameters MUST follow these structure requirements:

1. **No Frontmatter**: Files should NEVER contain frontmatter (the --- enclosed metadata sections)
2. **Direct Content**: All markdown content should begin directly with headers or text
3. **Standard Markdown**: Use only standard markdown formatting
4. **Header First**: Typically start with a level 1 header (# Title) followed by content 